Vita: --vita-fast-unseen-map=off|on (platform/vita/runtime/fast_painter.hpp). The minimap and the
map screen are drawn into their own framebuffer and copied to a texture (dRenderingMap_c::
renderingMap). The Vita backend has no offscreen framebuffer yet: it drops every draw sent to one,
and the copy, so the map never shows, but the game thread still wrote every polygon and line and
the GX worker still decoded them (54 to 351 dropped draws per frame on the console). While the
backend drops them, on leaves the path out; the framebuffer set-up, the back quad, the copy and
the 2D set-up after it are sent as before. Off (the default): nothing changes.

--- a/src/d/d_map_path.cpp
+++ b/src/d/d_map_path.cpp
@@ -414,8 +414,24 @@ void dRenderingMap_c::makeResTIMG(ResTIMG* p_image, u16 width, u16 height, u8* p
     p_image->imageOffset = p_data - (u8*)p_image;
 }
 
